cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Umax Guide Designer
message: >-
  If you use this tool, please cite the two publications the editor
  parameters are taken from, listed under references below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Varshney
    given-names: Gaurav K.
    affiliation: Oklahoma Medical Research Foundation, Oklahoma City, OK, USA
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/thevarshneylab/umax-guide-designer"
url: "https://thevarshneylab.github.io/umax-guide-designer/"
abstract: >-
  A browser-based sgRNA designer for zebrafish base editing with the
  ABE-Umax and TCBE-Umax editor families. Places a chosen target base
  within each editor's published editing window and reports bystander
  edits and codon-level consequences.
keywords:
  - CRISPR
  - base editing
  - zebrafish
  - sgRNA design
  - ABE-Umax
  - TCBE-Umax
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-19"
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      ABE-ultramax for high-efficiency biallelic adenine base editing in
      zebrafish
    authors:
      - family-names: Qin
        given-names: Wei
      - family-names: Varshney
        given-names: Gaurav K.
    journal: Nature Communications
    volume: 15
    start: 5613
    year: 2024
    doi: 10.1038/s41467-024-49943-1
  - type: article
    title: >-
      High-efficiency TadA cytosine base editors for precise modelling of
      human disease variants
    authors:
      - family-names: Qin
        given-names: Wei
      - family-names: Varshney
        given-names: Gaurav K.
    journal: Nature Biomedical Engineering
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.1038/s41551-025-01607-1
